                <pb facs="0610" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg604"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In accordance with instructions which I
                    have received from the Earl of Rosebery I have the honor to inclose copy of a
                    dispatch, together with its inclosures, which his lordship has addressed to Her
                    Majesty’s chargé d’affaires at Berlin, respecting the deportation of Mataafa and
                    other chiefs from Samoa.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
